      "writtenOn": "2025-03-20T08:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need `libartd-runtime_deps` and `libartd-runtime_deps`?",
      "revId": "e92b06c5fbdb735ca5bc8e72bcd652e37823ab79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb139396_1ec5160a",
        "filename": "runtime/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 666,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T12:12:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this is supposed to be `libartd-runtime_deps` and `libart_common_defaults`? If so then they are both used to try and keep the build command of the entrypoints as close to the non-simulator version (built as part of `libart-runtime_common_defaults`) as possible.\n\nWhile these additional arguments may not be used by the entrypoints, we\u0027d like to ensure that how we build the entrypoints for the simulator does not diverge from the regular non-simulator version. This would help if a build argument was added to `libartd-runtime_deps` or `libart_common_defaults` which did affect how the entrypoints were built.",
      "parentUuid": "ac5c1579_d4fe4e91",
      "revId": "e92b06c5fbdb735ca5bc8e72bcd652e37823ab79",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
